sec.p:
In addition to the activities provided in the digital-based lifestyle intervention, participants will also receive face-to-face group-based lifestyle intervention and individual-based lifestyle modification consultation. A total of 16 sessions of a group-based structured education program will be organized by trained local interventionists over a period of 36 months, with one session per month in the first 6 months and one session per quarter thereafter (Fig. 3). Slides for each group session will be developed by the Central Research Team at CAMS/PUMC. Before each session, researchers from the Central Research Team will train the local interventionists (physicians) within the local implementation team, and the session slides will be finalized collaboratively. The local implementation team will assess interventionists’ competency, focusing on their mastery of core content and their ability to effectively facilitate group sessions. All group sessions will be video-recorded and reviewed by the quality control personnel from both the local implementation team and the Central Research Team at CAMS/PUMC. Constructive feedback will be provided to ensure fidelity and consistency in intervention delivery. These sessions are designed to increase participants’ motivation, capability, and opportunity to change their behaviors. Each session follows a similar structure, including the following:
Warm-up to the meeting topic
Presentation of information on health consequences, outcome expectancies of the unhealthy lifestyle, and lifestyle changes related to the topic;
Risk perception and idea generation for lifestyle change, lifestyle goals recommendation, skills for change, role model from peers in the group;
Set up behavioral goals and develop action plan;
Identification of necessary source and help needed to carry out the plan;
Closing with commitment to action.Fig. 3
Schematic diagram schedule of interventions and time point assessments for Daqing DPS-II. The schematic diagram illustrates the intervention schedule, which consists of a core phase followed by a maintenance phase. The first 6 months constitute the core phase, during which participants receive monthly group sessions supplemented by follow-up telephone contacts, each occurring after the group session. This phase is designed to help participants achieve the targeted weight loss. From months 7 to 36, the intervention transitions to the maintenance phase, during which group sessions and telephone contacts are reduced to quarterly intervals to support weight loss maintenance and reinforce lifestyle behavior changes. Outcome assessments will be conducted at the 6 months, 12 months, 24 months, and 36 months
